    "page_title": "Transforming events in flight",
    "short_description": "Reshape, filter, and enrich events as they pass through a pipeline.",
    "body": "<h1>Transforming events in flight</h1>
<p>Once events enter your <a href="{{cms:item/5ac66235-69dc-4092-b430-9d68837e0c76}}">pipeline</a>, you can reshape them, filter out unwanted records, or add enrichment data from external sources — all before they reach their destination.</p>

<h2>Reshaping events</h2>
<p>Use a transform to extract, rename, or restructure fields from incoming events. Transforms are JavaScript functions that receive an event and return a modified version of it.</p>

{{ds:component/code-block|filename=transform.js|language=javascript|code=export default function transform(event) {
  return {
    user_id: event.customer_id,
    name: event.first_name + ' ' + event.last_name,
    email: event.contact_email,
    created_at: new Date(event.signup_timestamp).toISOString()
  };
}}}

<p>Return <code>null</code> from a transform to drop an event entirely, or throw an error to send it to the <a href="{{cms:item/062cc815-2b65-45b1-b36c-6ea67dfd1a0c}}">dead-letter queue</a>.</p>

<h2>Filtering events</h2>
<p>Add a filter condition to your transform to block unwanted records at the source. A filter that returns <code>false</code> discards the event; <code>true</code> passes it through.</p>

{{ds:component/code-block|filename=filter.js|language=javascript|code=export default function filter(event) {
  // Only pass through events from paying customers
  return event.plan_type !== 'free';
}}}

{{ds:component/alert|variant=info|title=Filters are fast|body_html=<p>Filtering in the pipeline is cheaper than transforming and sending to a destination, then filtering downstream. Apply filters early.</p>}}

<h2>Enriching with external data</h2>
<p>Your transform can call out to external APIs or databases to add data to each event. Be mindful of rate limits and latency — every enrichment call adds milliseconds to pipeline throughput.</p>

{{ds:component/code-block|filename=enrich.js|language=javascript|code=export default async function enrich(event) {
  const response = await fetch(`https://api.example.com/users/${event.user_id}`);
  const userData = await response.json();

  return {
    ...event,
    user_tier: userData.tier,
    account_balance: userData.balance
  };
}}}

{{ds:component/alert|variant=warning|title=Async transforms add latency|body_html=<p>Each external call blocks the pipeline for that event. Use with caution on high-throughput pipelines or consider batching lookups with a <a href="{{cms:item/dc9f1302-e173-4034-9581-d06efea7d090}}">scheduled task</a> instead.</p>}}

<h2>Chaining transforms</h2>
<p>A single transform stage can run multiple functions in sequence. The output of one becomes the input to the next.</p>

<h2>Monitoring transform failures</h2>
<p>If a transform throws, the event is retried according to your <a href="{{cms:item/062cc815-2b65-45b1-b36c-6ea67dfd1a0c}}">retry policy</a>. Watch transform error rates in <a href="{{cms:item/522ba05b-8a21-43dd-82ac-ece908ce14b4}}">Monitoring & alerts</a>.</p>

